# Trivy ignore file for known false positives and accepted risks
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# ── Rust crates embedded in compiled Polars .so (multiqc dependency) ──
# These live inside multiqc's prebuilt _polars_runtime.abi3.so; the fix requires
# Polars to release a build against the patched crate and multiqc to pull it, so
# no yml pin can reach the fix. Re-eval when multiqc ships a Polars with the fixes.
# quinn-proto: remote memory exhaustion via unbounded out-of-order stream reassembly
# (HIGH); fixed in 0.11.15, and the shipped .so carries 0.11.14. multiqc uses Polars
# only for local dataframe work over pipeline QC files and opens no QUIC connections.
GHSA-4w2j-m93h-cj5j exp:2026-11-15

# ── Go stdlib v1.23.4 in ncbi-datasets-cli 18.21.0 (ncbi_datasets container) ──
# The NCBI datasets/dataformat binaries are pre-compiled Go executables distributed
# via conda-forge. They ship Go stdlib v1.23.4; fixing everything below needs
# Go 1.26.10+ or 1.27.3+. We cannot rebuild these — only NCBI can, by updating
# their Go toolchain.
#
# Risk assessment: these binaries run in an isolated container that downloads
# genome metadata and sequences from NCBI over HTTPS and writes local files. They
# do not serve TLS or HTTP, connect to Postgres, or process untrusted archives — so
# the practical attack surface for these CVEs is minimal in our pipeline context.
#
# TODO: Remove these ignores when a newer ncbi-datasets-cli is available on
# conda-forge built with Go 1.26.10+ or 1.27.3+. Check with:
#   conda search -c conda-forge ncbi-datasets-cli
#   strings $(conda run -n <env> which datasets) | grep '^go1\.'
# Verified 2026-10-23: the latest conda-forge build (18.39.0) still ships Go stdlib
# go1.23.4 — identical to the pinned 18.21.0 — so bumping the pin fixes none of these.
# Confirmed by unpacking the conda package and running `strings` on datasets/dataformat.
#
# crypto/tls: resumed sessions skip certificate re-validation if the program mutates
# RootCAs/ClientCAs between handshakes (CRITICAL); exploiting it needs both that and a
# network attacker between the task and NCBI.
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-12-15
# net/url: memory exhaustion in query parameter parsing (HIGH)
CVE-2025-61726 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/x509: DoS via crafted certificate (HIGH)
CVE-2025-61729 exp:2026-12-15
# net/url: incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals (HIGH)
CVE-2026-25679 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/x509: DoS via excessive processing of DNS SAN entries in a crafted
# certificate (HIGH); these binaries validate only NCBI/AWS server certs.
CVE-2026-27145 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/x509: excessive CPU in certificate chain building (HIGH)
CVE-2026-32280 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/x509: DoS via inefficient certificate chain validation (HIGH)
CVE-2026-32281 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/tls: TLS 1.3 post-handshake key-update deadlock DoS (HIGH)
CVE-2026-32283 exp:2026-12-15
# net (cgo resolver): LookupCNAME mishandling of overlong CNAME responses (HIGH)
CVE-2026-33811 exp:2026-12-15
# net/http: HTTP/2 transport infinite loop on crafted SETTINGS frames (HIGH)
CVE-2026-33814 exp:2026-12-15
# net/mail: DoS via crafted ParseAddress/ParseAddressList/ParseDate inputs (HIGH)
CVE-2026-39820 exp:2026-12-15
# net: panic in Dial/LookupPort when handling NUL byte (HIGH)
CVE-2026-39836 exp:2026-12-15
# net/mail: DoS via pathological consumePhrase inputs (HIGH)
CVE-2026-42499 exp:2026-12-15
# mime/net-mail: excessive CPU decoding crafted MIME headers with many invalid
# encoded-words (HIGH); these CLIs fetch JSON from NCBI's API, never parse email/MIME.
CVE-2026-42504 exp:2026-12-15
# encoding/asn1: DoS via excessive recursion in Unmarshal (HIGH); ASN.1 parsing here is
# limited to NCBI/AWS server certificates.
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-12-15
# golang.org/x/net/idna: privilege escalation via incorrect Punycode label processing
# (HIGH); hostnames are the hardcoded NCBI/AWS endpoints, not attacker-supplied.
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-12-15
# os.Root: symlink following allows directory traversal (HIGH); these binaries write to
# the workflow's own task directory, with no untrusted symlink sources.
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-12-15
# net/http: unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to DoS (HIGH); all traffic is
# client-side HTTPS to NCBI/AWS.
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-12-15
# html/template: XSS via pathological input (HIGH); no server-side templating in these
# client-only CLI tools.
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-12-15
# encoding/xml: DoS via XML decoding recursion depth (HIGH); these CLIs consume JSON
# from NCBI's API, not XML.
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-12-15
# net/url: DoS from quadratic complexity in path resolution (HIGH); URLs are constructed
# by the tools themselves against known endpoints.
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/tls: DoS via indefinite KeyUpdate messages (HIGH); requires a hostile TLS peer,
# and these binaries talk only to NCBI/AWS.
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-12-15
# net/http: CPU DoS via crafted Range headers in FileServer/ServeContent (HIGH);
# server-side only, and these binaries serve no HTTP.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-12-15
# net/http2: CPU DoS from a hostile HTTP/2 peer flooding SETTINGS frames (HIGH); needs
# a malicious NCBI endpoint or network attacker, and the worst case is a failed task.
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-12-15
# crypto/tls: server memory exhaustion via repeated ECH outer-extension references
# (HIGH); server-side only.
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-12-15

# ── Debian trixie base image (mambaorg/micromamba): no fixes reachable ──
# The base-image knob (container-base-image in pyproject.toml) is the only
# permitted lever for these system packages, and as of 2026-10-23 Debian has no
# trixie fix for any of them (<no-dsa> or <postponed>), so no base-image bump
# reaches one. The generated Dockerfiles set USER root, so local privilege-
# escalation flaws have no less-privileged user to start from. Re-eval when
# Debian ships a trixie fix (then bump the digest and drop the entry).

# ncurses: stack-based buffer overflow in infocmp CLI tool (no-dsa, low urgency)
# Our containers never invoke infocmp. Fix only in sid (6.6+).
CVE-2025-69720 exp:2026-12-15

# acl (libacl1): symlink-traversal privilege escalation in the pathname-based
# acl_*_file() functions (HIGH). Debian's coreutils links libacl1, so commands like
# cp may reach them, but exploiting it needs a less-privileged local user who swaps
# a path component for a symlink while a privileged process handles it; tasks run
# as root with no other users. Debian will fix it in sid first, then in a trixie
# point release.
CVE-2026-54369 exp:2026-12-15

# systemd-homed: local privilege escalation via missing home-record signature
# verification (HIGH). libsystemd0 is only a library dependency; no container runs
# systemd or systemd-homed.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-12-15

# util-linux 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 (mount, libmount1, bsdutils, …): four local privilege-
# escalation flaws in mount(8) and nsenter (all HIGH) — X-mount post-hooks running
# after a failed mount helper, X-mount.subdir escaping via intermediate symlinks,
# restricted bind mounts not pinning their source, and nsenter --join-cgroup leaking
# a root cgroup fd. All need an unprivileged user running mount or nsenter; the
# pipeline invokes neither, and tasks already run as root.
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-12-15

# ── urllib3 < 2.8.0: via awscli in blast, bowtie2_samtools, kraken2,
# minimap2_samtools; vendored by pip in pysam_biopython ──
# Our awscli usage is `update_blastdb.pl --source aws` in the BLAST container —
# HTTPS to known NCBI/AWS endpoints, no proxy, no attacker-controlled compressed
# streams. No module script invokes awscli in the other three containers, and
# nothing runs pip at run time. Every conda-forge awscli build through 2.38.1 pins
# urllib3<=2.6.3, and pip 26.2.2 (the newest) vendors urllib3 2.7.0, so no pin
# reaches the 2.8.0 fix. Re-eval when the awscli feedstock relaxes the cap and pip
# re-vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
# CVE-2026-44431 (HIGH, awscli only): cross-origin header leak in proxied low-level redirects.
CVE-2026-44431 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-44432 (HIGH, awscli only): decompression-bomb safeguard bypass in streaming reads.
CVE-2026-44432 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-97687 (HIGH): HTTPS-proxy connections inherit target-server TLS settings such
# as CERT_NONE; needs an HTTPS proxy, and no task configures one.
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-97689 (HIGH): unbounded memory in the chunked-response parser; needs a
# malicious server, and the worst case is an out-of-memory task.
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-12-15

# ── perl-base (Debian trixie 5.40.1-6+deb13u1): fix postponed as of 2026-10-23 ──
# The pipeline's only perl invocation is `update_blastdb.pl` in the maintainer-run
# INDEX step (modules/local/downloadBlastDB), which fetches official NCBI/AWS BLAST
# databases via `--source aws`. perl-base is otherwise present only as a Debian
# base-image dependency, not called by any pipeline tool. None of these CVEs is
# reachable on attacker-controlled input in that context. Re-eval: Debian backports
# a fix to trixie perl-base (a rebuild then clears them), or the pipeline gains a
# perl path that processes untrusted tar/regex/glob input.
# Archive::Tar unbounded allocation -> memory-exhaustion DoS (HIGH); trusted tarballs, worst case ephemeral OOM.
CVE-2026-9538 exp:2026-12-15

# ── pip's vendored dependencies (pysam_biopython) ──
# msgpack out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse after a caught error, and a setuptools
# PackageIndex path traversal (both HIGH). Neither is our dependency: they are reported
# from pip's own vendored bundle at site-packages/pip/_vendor (vendor.txt / bom.cdx.json),
# not from the conda environment, which does not install either package. pip 26.2.2 is
# already the newest release and still vendors msgpack 1.1.2, so no pin can reach it;
# the setuptools entry is SBOM metadata only, with no setuptools code under _vendor at all.
# pip's vendored msgpack is used by cachecontrol to serialise pip's HTTP cache, reached
# only when pip downloads packages -- the pipeline never invokes pip at run time.
# Re-eval: a pip release that re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1 (then drop these two).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-30
